(in-ns 'go.arbace.py) ^{:go/comments [[3 1 "// The dispatch loop (doc/python/PYI-SPEC.md §7.5): one loop per entry from Go, running frames until"] [4 1 "// the entry frame returns. A call of a Python function pushes its frame and continues; a return pops"] [5 1 "// it. An exception unwinds by the exception table: the covering handler's depth, lasti and target,"] [6 1 "// else the frame is left and the caller's instruction raises it."] [8 1 "// guardedStep is step with a Go panic of the runtime turned into a SystemError raised at f's instruction"] [9 1 "// (REQUEST of PY6g for PY6-core, PY6a's Low: a panic ended the whole lib-test module, now only its test)"] [14 31 "// the C-level checks' increments the panic skipped"] [15 31 "// and a direct call's (queue 216d), had the panic crossed one"] [20 3 "// step's own frame not entered for compiled code (queue 216d); while tracing, the loop (queue 219t): a compiled"] [21 3 "// frame hands itself over at a block start (AotToLoop)"] [29 1 "// run runs f (and the frames it calls) to f's return: Go's call into the machine, CPython's"] [30 1 "// _PyEval_EvalFrameDefault entered from C, the C level's recursion check first (where \"\", PY7)."] [41 1 "// runFrames is run's loop, f its entry frame. direct (queue 216d): f is a callee a compiled caller runs from its own Go"] [42 1 "// code (callDirect) where it would have returned f as its *pushFrame: f entered as this loop enters a pushed frame,"] [43 1 "// the eval breaker's error raised in f, and no C level counted (a Python call is none: run's check is Go's entry)."] [47 18 "// f_back of an escaped frame reaches its callers (202b)"] [55 31 "// a direct callee's RESUME error, raised in it as in a pushed frame"] [56 31 "// RESUME: the eval breaker (PY6f's thread_gil.go)"] [65 41 "// sys.monitoring's PY_START, PY_RESUME, PY_THROW (queue 220; breakMonitor)"] [78 37 "// PY_RETURN, PY_YIELD (queue 220): a callback's error raised in f"] [82 4 "// f returned v"] [90 21 "// a suspended generator's f_back is None (its caller may be reused: releaseFrame)"] [98 5 "// callInit's __init__ returned: the instance is the call's value (type_call's check of __init__'s)"] [111 4 "// a call of a Python function from f: run the callee in this loop"] [126 5 "// the callee's RESUME: the eval breaker (PY6f's thread_gil.go), its error raised in the callee; then"] [127 5 "// sys.monitoring's PY_START (queue 220: breakMonitor keeps the breaker set while a tool has events)"] [138 3 "// an exception in f at f.Lasti"] [144 4 "// an exception the runtime raised in f (a KeyError of d[k] ...): chained as _PyErr_SetObject chains"] [149 23 "// a re-raise adds no entry for the frame it is raised in (exception_unwind)"] [153 38 "// RAISE (queue 219t): settrace's 'exception'"] [162 47 "// frame->instr_ptr: a reraise N's restored instruction"] [168 24 "// PY_UNWIND (queue 220)"] [181 1 "// OpImpl implements an operation outside step's switch (PYI-SPEC.md §7.5): it pops and pushes f's"] [182 1 "// stack itself and returns (nil, nil) to go on; (nil, err) raises; (nil, *pushFrame) runs a Python"] [183 1 "// function's frame next; (v, nil) makes f return v (a generator's yield sets f.Suspended first)."] [186 1 "// opImpls are the operations registered by the files that own them (§9), each by its file's init:"] [187 1 "// RegisterOp(OpLoadAttr, ...). An operation of step's switch is never looked up here."] [190 1 "// RegisterOp sets op's implementation; a second one is a programming error (one owner per operation)."] [198 1 "// pushFrame is step's signal that the instruction called a Python function: not an exception."] [201 1 "// callStack is call [N KWNAMES]: the callable under its N arguments on f's stack (the last len(kwnames) of them"] [202 1 "// keywords), all popped; a Python function's frame (a bound method's, its self first) made from the arguments"] [203 1 "// where they are on the stack and returned as the thread's *pushFrame, a generator made, or any other callable"] [204 1 "// called and its value pushed (202b: the arguments were copied off the stack, then again with self in front)."] [206 22 "// sys.monitoring's CALL, C_RETURN, C_RAISE (queue 220)"] [218 24 "// the callable's slot holds self: the arguments are self's and the stack's"] [230 4 "// a built-in method bound to its object (BuiltinType's call slot): its arguments made at once with self"] [231 4 "// first (queue 210: they were copied off the stack, then again behind self)"] [260 3 "// CPython's RETURN_GENERATOR: the frame kept in its generator, coroutine or async generator"] [267 1 "// directMax bounds the direct calls (callDirect) nested on the thread's Go stack at once: each holds its caller's Go"] [268 1 "// frames while its callee runs, so a deeper chain (a recursion past it, up to any recursion limit) goes on as pushed"] [269 1 "// frames, in the innermost loop, with no Go frames per Python call (queue 216d)."] [272 1 "// enter is a call's callee frame (made, its arguments bound) run from f: when f and the callee are both compiled,"] [273 1 "// directly by f's own Go code (callDirect: its value pushed on f's stack, or its exception returned); else returned"] [274 1 "// as the thread's *pushFrame, read by runFrames before the thread's next call."] [283 1 "// callDirect runs callee, a compiled function's frame called by f's compiled code (queue 216d, the user's (a) on"] [284 1 "// 216's DECISION 1): a loop of its own (runFrames, direct) with callee its entry frame, entered as runFrames enters a"] [285 1 "// pushed frame (f_back f, the recursion limit's check raising in f, the eval breaker's error in callee, no C level),"] [286 1 "// so its exception unwinds through callee's handlers and leaves it with callee's traceback entry, then f's code"] [287 1 "// returns it and f's loop adds f's; its value pushed on f's stack, or callInit's instance (an __init__ returning"] [288 1 "// anything but None the TypeError raised in f), as runFrames pushes a returning pushed frame's."] [298 1 "// runDirect is callDirect's run of callee from the running frame's compiled code: its value (callInit's instance for"] [299 1 "// an __init__), or its exception, returned to that code."] [318 1 "// callInit is the call of a class whose __init__ runs in the caller's loop (initInline; queue 210, CPython 3.14's"] [319 1 "// CALL_ALLOC_AND_ENTER_INIT): the instance made by the type's __new__ (object's) from the arguments where they are"] [320 1 "// on f's stack (k the first's position), then __init__'s frame with the instance as self in the class's slot,"] [321 1 "// returned as the thread's *pushFrame; runFrames pushes the instance when that frame returns None (TypeType's call"] [322 1 "// slot's check otherwise, raised at the call)."] [340 1 "// initInline is the __init__ a call of t (its metatype type) runs in the caller's loop (callInit): the Python"] [341 1 "// function __init__ resolves to, when t and every class of its MRO but object are class statements' (no built-in"] [342 1 "// layout), __new__ resolves to object's and __init__ is not a generator's or a coroutine's; nil otherwise, and the"] [343 1 "// call goes through TypeType's call slot. Kept on t while typeEpoch has not moved."] [371 1 "// kwnamesAt is a call's keyword names, the tuple constant i of str (-1: none), made once."] [393 1 "// step runs f's instructions until it returns (the value, nil), raises (nil, error), or calls a"] [394 1 "// Python function (nil, *pushFrame)."] [398 3 "// compiled ahead (PY8, aot.go): the same frame, from f.PC; while tracing, the loop (queue 219t)"] [404 36 "// the line, opcode and jump events (queue 219t, trace.go)"] [772 24 "// CALL, and a C callable's C_RETURN or C_RAISE (queue 220)"] [793 6 "// CPython's RETURN_GENERATOR: the frame kept in its generator, coroutine or async generator"] [832 33 "// a function made where the globals are a mapping has them too (func_globals)"] [851 52 "// JUMP_BACKWARD: the eval breaker"] [882 5 "// a generator run to its end with a value other than None: the StopIteration gen_iternext sets, RAISE"] [883 5 "// (the instrumented FOR_ITER's monitor_raise; queue 219t)"] [893 65 "// raised by Python code: RAISE (queue 219t)"] [898 24 "// FOR_ITER clears a raised StopIteration: the loop's end"] [920 5 "// RERAISE N: the lasti N items down is where the frame reports itself (f_lineno)"] [926 4 "// the traceback continues: the handler's frame is already in it"] [960 3 "// globals not a dict but a subclass's instance (FunctionType(code, globals), exec, eval; queue 205f): its"] [961 3 "// __getitem__, a KeyError not found (LOAD_GLOBAL's and LOAD_FROM_DICT_OR_GLOBALS' PyMapping_GetOptionalItem)"] [972 1 "// globalIC is load-global's inline cache (queue 210; CPython's LOAD_GLOBAL_MODULE and LOAD_GLOBAL_BUILTIN, by the"] [973 1 "// dicts' keys version): the globals it last saw and where the name was: in the globals at entry gi, or (gi -1)"] [974 1 "// absent from them at their version gver and in the builtins b at entry bi. An entry is the name's while it holds"] [975 1 "// the name's very str (names are interned: co_names, and a module's and the builtins' names, through nameStr), so a"] [976 1 "// hit reads the entry's current value; the globals' absence holds while their version, moved by every insertion and"] [977 1 "// deletion, has not."] [984 1 "// loadGlobalAt is load-global of name at f's instruction pc (loadGlobal through the instruction's cache)."] [1034 1 "// loadNameGlobal is LOAD_NAME's lookup after the locals: the globals' dict itself (_PyEval_LoadName's"] [1035 1 "// PyDict_GetItemRef: a dict subclass's __missing__ not called), then the builtins."] [1059 1 "// doRaise is raise (0: re-raise the handled exception; 1: raise exc; 2: raise exc from cause)."] [1076 3 "// do_raise's cause (Python/ceval.c): a class called (its result an instance), an instance, None, else TypeError"] [1101 1 "// makeException is raise's operand as an exception: an instance, or a class called with no arguments."] 